  "intro": [
   "If you're into Sasquatch this is the trip. It starts in Harrison Hot Springs, BC, which basically built its whole identity around the Sasquatch (there's a museum, a provincial park and a festival), then heads down through Vancouver, Seattle and the Mount St. Helens country where the Ape Canyon attack story comes from.",
   "From Portland it's south to the North American Bigfoot Center in Boring, Oregon, then all the way down to Willow Creek and the Bluff Creek area, home of the 1958 footprints and the Patterson-Gimlin film. Bring good boots and a lot of patience for winding roads."
